{
  "requirement": "Every {term}`requirements.sdk.application_domain` implements\n`trust_but_verify::domain::Domain`. A domain is cloneable and safe to share between\nexecutions. The following chapters introduce its members one capability at a\ntime.\n\n```rust,ignore\npub trait Domain: Clone + Send + Sync {\n    type Error: Send;\n    type NodeId: Clone + Eq + Send + Sync;\n    type NodeContent: NodeContents;\n    type EdgeLabel: Clone + Send + Sync;\n\n    fn node_path(&self, node: &Self::NodeId) -> NodePath;\n    fn node_content(\n        &self,\n        node: &Self::NodeId,\n    ) -> Result<Self::NodeContent, Self::Error>;\n    fn outgoing_edges(\n        &self,\n        node: &Self::NodeId,\n        label: Self::EdgeLabel,\n    ) -> Result<Vec<Self::NodeId>, Self::Error>;\n    fn load_evidence(\n        &self,\n        node: &Self::NodeId,\n        criterion: &CriterionPath,\n    ) -> impl Future<Output = Result<Option<Record<Self::NodeId, Self::EdgeLabel>>, Self::Error>> + Send;\n    fn store_evidence(\n        &self,\n        node: &Self::NodeId,\n        criterion: &CriterionPath,\n        record: &Record<Self::NodeId, Self::EdgeLabel>,\n    ) -> impl Future<Output = Result<(), Self::Error>> + Send;\n}\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The subject `requirements.sdk.domain` mainly specifies the shape of the `Domain` trait. That covers its bounds, associated types, five methods, and the Send futures. It also says a domain is cloneable and safe to share between executions.\n\n**Trait shape and bounds.** The test `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/contracts.rs#fn[domain_relationships_accept_opaque_types_and_send_only_errors]` covers this.\n- It implements `Domain` for a fixture whose types carry only the minimum bounds. `Identity` is Clone, PartialEq and Eq. `Label` is Clone only. `GraphError` wraps a `Cell`, so it is Send but not Sync, Debug, Clone or `std::error::Error`. That would fail to compile if the trait added any of those bounds.\n- The generic `check_bounds::<G: Domain>` helper requires `Clone + Send + Sync` of the domain, `Clone + Eq + Send + Sync` of `NodeId`, `Clone + Send + Sync` of `EdgeLabel`, `Send` of `Error`, and `NodeContents` of `NodeContent`. It would fail to compile if the trait loosened any of these bounds.\n\n**Methods.** The same test calls all five methods and asserts their results.\n- `node_path` is asserted to return the expected segments, and distinct paths are checked for distinct nodes.\n- `outgoing_edges` is asserted for duplicates and order, for different labels, for empty results, and for an error case.\n- The error value is passed through `send(error)` and its payload is checked.\n- `node_content` is asserted through `format()` and `fingerprint()`.\n- `load_evidence` and `store_evidence` are driven through `send(...)`, which requires Send futures even with a non-Sync error. Their results are asserted: `load_evidence` returns `None`, and `store_evidence` succeeds.\n\n**Cloneable and shareable between executions.** Several marked tests clone the domain into a `Validator` and run executions concurrently:\n- `contracts.rs#fn[concurrent_same_criterion_executions_keep_complete_independent_records]`\n- `validation.rs#fn[concurrent_single_node_validations_keep_separate_traces]`\n- `validation.rs#fn[shared_context_allows_independent_concurrent_agent_calls]`\n- `agent/tests.rs#fn[concurrent_tool_agents_isolate_histories_pages_and_submissions_and_share_reads]`\n\nThese tests assert that records, traces and results stay separate across concurrent executions. The compile-time Send+Sync+Clone check in `check_bounds` supports them.\n\n**Other marked tests.** `contracts.rs#fn[criteria_keep_typed_answers_and_persist_only_when_requested]` exercises the evidence storage path. The tests in `agent/tests.rs` and `src/sdk.rs` exercise the contents and evidence path with domain implementations.\n\nI found no obligation that lacks a test. The `application_domain` definition only cites the requirement and imposes nothing further.",
  "references": "f134ef8b59e6ae40d7fbe7c03caa0da74ab64ddcf0c0ab2781b1bf2f56e64fec",
